{"actor":"model","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-137182","model_call":15,"attempt":1,"model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input_tokens":7361,"output_tokens":197,"total_tokens":7558,"cached_tokens":6400,"reasoning_tokens":41},"output_characters":698,"decision":{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_642027397#0_1410055885","relevance":3,"reason":"The result is dedicated to explaining social engineering scams and directly states that fraudsters dupe victims through psychological manipulation, a confidence trick that influences people to take actions not in their best interest.","learned":"For cybercrime to appeal to a victim can mean using trust and psychological manipulation to influence the victim into acting against their own interest."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1991","reason":"The current social-engineering query is highly productive for direct evidence on victim manipulation and appeals, so continue for more grade-3 results."}}}
