{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-137182","model_call":30,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1991"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1991"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_749830055#1_1726160666","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1991","rank":24,"snippet":"5. Be Cautious of Foreign Offers How to Protect Yourself from Social Engineering Attacks? Incognito Forensic Foundation (IFF Lab) – Your Awareness & Diagnostic Partner Contact us for Awareness Programs and Investigation Services. \" , \"segment\": \"It is a technique used by cyber criminals to defraud innocent victims. Here’s all that you need to know about social engineering attack techniques. Also, some handy tips to avoid being a social engineering <cover>victim. What is Social Engineering? Social Engineering is the trending technique for trapping gullible individuals into divulging their personal information. Rightly called ‘social engineering’ as it exploits a person’s natural tendency to trust another individual. Social Engineering is more of an art! Know why? Because it requires a certain mastery to manipulate </cover>people into entrusting another individual, usually a stranger, with personal information. Miscreants find it easier to employ social engineering to gain personal information than use traditional techniques such as hacking.\" , \"start_char\": 522.000000 , \"title\": \"Top 5 Social Engineering Attack Techniques Used by Cyber Criminals\" , \"url\": \"https://ifflab.org/top-5-social-engineering-attack-techniques-used-"},"time":15},"model_calls":30,"document_judgments":27,"relevance_3":24,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
